rs ${q}_{1},{q}_{2},{q}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{2}+{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{3}=\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{3}-{q}_{1}+2{q}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}=3{q}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}=-2{q}_{1}+2{q}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{3}=4{q}_{1}-8{q}_{2}+4{q}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, this system can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {q}_{1} & {q}_{2} & {q}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{r}_{11}+{r}_{12}+{r}_{33}=3+(-2)+4=5.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "668df193-99f3-547e-8195-6dfa92ee8c3d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442811}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442814 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442810 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3529dcc2-d908-58eb-8e99-7d1d828d18b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442804} {:answer/id #uuid "387b9ac5-2487-5c7a-a0c7-85adba10d944" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442805} {:answer/id #uuid "af55c525-fcb4-5409-9a04-32dc1d2a0e2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442806} {:answer/id #uuid "bf0166a7-27f9-57f1-b2b0-ed7ed1491514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442807} {:answer/id #uuid "c403d147-73fe-5fb4-8186-c08fd069f494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442808}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442807} :answer-field/id #uuid "b927eac4-98a6-5bd4-97b1-9da46ea6a1a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442809}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "71405c00-ca6f-5d4e-8940-325d2e48014e" :question/math-academy-id "q-40841" :question/problem "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{q}_{11} & {q}_{12} \\\\ {q}_{21} & {q}_{22} \\\\ {q}_{31} & {q}_{32}\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}}}.\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above. Given that the columns ${q}_{1},{q}_{2}$ of $Q$ were obtained from the columns of $A$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, find  the value of ${q}_{32}\\cdot {r}_{12}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ be the columns of $A.$\n\nFirst, we find an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ using the Gram-Schmidt process.\n\n**Step 1**. We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**. We find the vector ${v}_{2}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1}\\}$ using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{6}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we normalize ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {q}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}A \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{3} & 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following QR factorization of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{3} & 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{bmatrix}}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, ${q}_{32}\\cdot {r}_{12}=(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}})\\cdot (2\\sqrt{3})=\\sqrt{2}.$"} :step/id #uuid "73796bfe-825e-5f2c-aa11-3af559c65185" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442812}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442815 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364620 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87e36d9c-e9a2-5446-ad66-2c509425fb2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364622} {:answer/id #uuid "6838046c-6bb6-5382-aff4-79052bb83389" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364623} {:answer/id #uuid "66729efb-cb03-5e0d-975f-24a9597e8440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364624} {:answer/id #uuid "0e78a432-6e13-5220-8bcd-195f0ec965d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364625} {:answer/id #uuid "eac12345-022f-5cbe-aa4a-767d1ed83136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364626}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364624} :answer-field/id #uuid "736f5b90-2f10-5a15-8216-cf8f1586fc1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5c7952d1-1f1c-50a2-a342-5271912d43de" :question/math-academy-id "q-96033" :question/problem "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{q}_{11} & {q}_{12} \\\\ {q}_{21} & {q}_{22} \\\\ {q}_{31} & {q}_{32}\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}}}.\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above. Given that the columns ${q}_{1},{q}_{2}$ of $Q$ were obtained from the columns of $A$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, find  the value of ${q}_{12}\\cdot {r}_{22}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ be the columns of $A.$\n\nFirst, we find an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ using the Gram-Schmidt process.\n\n**Step 1**. We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**. We find the vector ${v}_{2}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1}\\}$ using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}-(-\\frac{6}{18})\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we normalize ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {q}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}\\,A \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 & 3\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following QR factorization of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 & 3\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, ${q}_{12}\\cdot {r}_{22}=(\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}})\\cdot (3\\sqrt{2})=4.$"} :step/id #uuid "aaefce95-2575-5d4e-9758-6032bf02fe49"}] :activity/title "QR Factorization" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442803}]}
